2. Two Sum II:

Code:
class Solution {
    public int[] twoSum(int[] numbers, int target) {
        int left = 0;
        int right = numbers.length - 1;

        while (left < right) {
            int sum = numbers[left] + numbers[right];

            if (sum == target) {
                return new int[]{left + 1, right + 1};
            } 
            else if (sum < target) {
                left++;
            } 
            else {
                right--;
            }
        }

        return new int[]{-1, -1};
    }
}

Approach:
Use the two-pointer technique because the array is sorted. Start with pointers at both ends: if the sum is less than the target, move left forward; if greater, move right backward until the target is found.

Complexity:
Time: O(n) — each pointer moves at most n times.
Space: O(1) — only two pointer variables are used.

